1
00:00:00,195 --> 00:00:02,995
(Sheldon:)Oh.
Yeah, this little guy

2
00:00:02,998 --> 00:00:04,368
(Sheldon:)can already recognize

3
00:00:04,366 --> 00:00:06,096
(Sheldon:)electronically
transmitted images

4
00:00:06,101 --> 00:00:09,401
(Sheldon:)20% faster than any other
sample in Amy's lab.

5
00:00:10,238 --> 00:00:12,268
(Bernadette:)I'm running out of ways
to act excited.

6
00:00:14,509 --> 00:00:17,609
(Amy:)So, enough about us,
how are things going with you?

7
00:00:17,612 --> 00:00:19,382
(Bernadette:)Great, the doctor
said the baby's head

8
00:00:19,381 --> 00:00:20,581
(Bernadette:)is facing down now.

9
00:00:20,582 --> 00:00:22,012
(Amy:)Good, you know,

10
00:00:22,017 --> 00:00:24,687
(Amy:)in case the exit
isn't clearly marked.

11
00:00:24,686 --> 00:00:28,126
(Sheldon:)Yeah, I have to say,
it is nice to share

12
00:00:28,123 --> 00:00:31,253
(Sheldon:)this experience with someone
who's on the same journey.

13
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:36,000
(Sheldon:)Although right now ours
is testing off the charts

14
00:00:35,997 --> 00:00:39,097
(Sheldon:)while yours is floating
around in its own waste.

15
00:00:40,535 --> 00:00:43,605
(Bernadette:)Are you actually comparing
my human baby

16
00:00:43,605 --> 00:00:46,105
(Bernadette:)to your brain in a bowl?

17
00:00:47,142 --> 00:00:48,472
(Sheldon:)Well, I didn't
make you waddle up

18
00:00:48,476 --> 00:00:50,806
(Sheldon:)four flights of stairs
for the heck of it.

19
00:00:51,980 --> 00:00:54,750
(Bernadette:)You do realize my baby
has functioning organs

20
00:00:54,749 --> 00:00:56,349
(Bernadette:)and can recognize voices.

21
00:00:56,351 --> 00:00:59,481
(Sheldon:)Yeah, but ours can recognize
a specific data stream

